{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JGokPjLacdPBTZvxXchgT5","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→Implement the share_docs feature for the Vista dashboard based on the implementation plan at .vista/ralph/share-docs-plan/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md\n     2→\n     3→Follow the plan's 6 steps in order:\n     4→\n     5→1. Add `read_domain_requirements()` to `vista/server/services/progress_service.py`\n     6→2. Create `vista/server/services/export_service.py` with `ExportService` class\n     7→3. Create `vista/server/routes/export.py` with GET/POST endpoints + register router in `vista/server/app.py`\n     8→4. Create `vista/server/views/export.html` — self-contained HTML export template (standalone, NOT extending _base.html). Must include full JS for Mermaid rendering, pan/zoom, modal expand, and marked.js requirements rendering. Copy CSS/JS patterns from `vista/server/views/architecture.html`.\n     9→5. Add Export modal + button to `vista/server/views/project.html` — tree-style checklist with per-diagram selection\n    10→6. Create `vista/tests/test_export_service.py` with unit tests\n    11→\n    12→Key requirements:\n    13→- Exported HTML must work without any server — all content embedded, libraries via CDN\n    14→- Embed diagram/requirements data as JSON via |tojson filter, render client-side\n    15→- Match Vista dark theme from architecture.html\n    16→- Card gallery with modal overlay for expanded diagrams\n    17→- Tree checklist in export modal: features as parents, diagrams as children, indeterminate state support\n    18→\n    19→Reference the implementation plan for exact code, file locations, and codebase references."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c06c8987-38bb-4a43-9247-2ef00a647fd1","uuid":"6db91bf8-18c8-4fea-b765-8be989c26665","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/Users/Grove/OneDrive/Documents/PYTHON/claude_plugins/vista/.vista/ralph/share-docs-build/task.md","content":"Implement the share_docs feature for the Vista dashboard based on the implementation plan at .vista/ralph/share-docs-plan/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md\n\nFollow the plan's 6 steps in order:\n\n1. Add `read_domain_requirements()` to `vista/server/services/progress_service.py`\n2. Create `vista/server/services/export_service.py` with `ExportService` class\n3. Create `vista/server/routes/export.py` with GET/POST endpoints + register router in `vista/server/app.py`\n4. Create `vista/server/views/export.html` — self-contained HTML export template (standalone, NOT extending _base.html). Must include full JS for Mermaid rendering, pan/zoom, modal expand, and marked.js requirements rendering. Copy CSS/JS patterns from `vista/server/views/architecture.html`.\n5. Add Export modal + button to `vista/server/views/project.html` — tree-style checklist with per-diagram selection\n6. Create `vista/tests/test_export_service.py` with unit tests\n\nKey requirements:\n- Exported HTML must work without any server — all content embedded, libraries via CDN\n- Embed diagram/requirements data as JSON via |tojson filter, render client-side\n- Match Vista dark theme from architecture.html\n- Card gallery with modal overlay for expanded diagrams\n- Tree checklist in export modal: features as parents, diagrams as children, indeterminate state support\n\nReference the implementation plan for exact code, file locations, and codebase references.","numLines":19,"startLine":1,"totalLines":19}}}
